<section class="page-intro accent-ticket">
  <p class="eyebrow">Build / How we work</p><h1>One founder. A team of agents. Everything written down.</h1><p class="lede">We build in the open about how, and carefully about what. One person decides; a team of AI agents, each with one job, specifies, builds, reviews and tests.</p><p class="status">Work in progress</p>
</section>
<section class="editorial section">
  <h2>How decisions get made</h2>
  <div class="prose">
    <p>The founder decides what gets built. Each decision is recorded in her own words, so there is always a plain answer to “why is it like this?”</p><p>Nothing ships on a summary. Money, access and tax work gets a security review before it merges, and the founder installs each build herself, with a way back ready.</p>
  </div>
</section>
<section class="evidence-panel" aria-labelledby="status-title">
  <p class="eyebrow">Where things stand</p><h2 id="status-title">What it does on a shift, in three lists.</h2>
  <div class="evidence-grid">
    <div>
      <h3>Built</h3>
      <ul class="status-list">
        <li>Take orders on a register, an iPad or a phone, and add to a check that has already gone to the kitchen.</li>
        <li>Send orders to the kitchen screen and to the kitchen and receipt printers. The kitchen sees only what is new.</li>
        <li>Floor plans by room, with the tables where they really are.</li>
        <li>Sold-out items, and “only a few left” counts, right on the menu.</li>
        <li>A time clock with corrections, side work lists, and a shift log for handover notes.</li>
        <li>Close the day with a check of open checks and the cash you should have.</li>
        <li>Reports that add up to what each bill actually charged.</li>
        <li>Roles that say who may do what, with every change on the record.</li>
        <li>Your records stay on a machine you own. Nothing leaves it unless the owner turns it on.</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
    <div>
      <h3>In the works</h3>
      <ul class="status-list">
        <li>A new look across the iPad, the phone and the handheld, so a table’s check feels the same wherever you open it.</li>
        <li>“My checks”: each person’s own checks, handed over cleanly when a shift changes.</li>
        <li>Seats and split checks, and one dish sent to two kitchen stations.</li>
        <li>Paid and unpaid breaks on the time clock.</li>
        <li>A lighter mode for older devices.</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
    <div>
      <h3>Coming</h3>
      <ul class="status-list">
        <li>Courses, and a way back when a printer stops mid-service.</li>
        <li>Approvals from a phone, staff invites, and device settings.</li>
        <li>Card payments.</li>
        <li>A live view of the tip pool, so everyone in it sees their share.</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </div>
